{"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Central-Manager","identifiers":["doc:\/\/iOS-BLE-Library\/documentation\/iOS_BLE_Library\/ReactiveCentralManagerDelegate"],"title":"Central Manager","generated":true}],"metadata":{"fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"CentralManager","kind":"identifier"}],"symbolKind":"class","roleHeading":"Class","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"CentralManager","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","title":"CentralManager","modules":[{"name":"iOS_BLE_Library"}],"externalID":"s:15iOS_BLE_Library14CentralManagerC"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/iOS-BLE-Library\/documentation\/iOS_BLE_Library"]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ios_ble_library\/centralmanager"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"CentralManager"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"It wraps the standard CBCentralManager and has similar API. However, instead of using delegate, it uses publishers, thus bringing the reactive programming paradigm to the CoreBluetooth framework.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Create-a-Central-Manager","type":"heading","text":"Create a Central Manager","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/iOS-BLE-Library\/documentation\/iOS_BLE_Library\/CentralManager"},{"type":"text","text":" is merely a wrapper around "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CBCentralManager"},{"type":"text","text":" with an instance of it inside."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The new instance of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CBCentralManager"},{"type":"text","text":" can be created during initialization using "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/iOS-BLE-Library\/documentation\/iOS_BLE_Library\/CentralManager\/init(centralManagerDelegate:queue:options:)"},{"type":"text","text":", or an existing instance can be passed using "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/iOS-BLE-Library\/documentation\/iOS_BLE_Library\/CentralManager\/init(centralManager:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you pass a central manager inside "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/iOS-BLE-Library\/documentation\/iOS_BLE_Library\/CentralManager\/init(centralManager:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", it should already have a delegate set. The delegate should be an instance of "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/iOS-BLE-Library\/documentation\/iOS_BLE_Library\/ReactiveCentralManagerDelegate","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"; otherwise, an error will be thrown."}]},{"anchor":"Use-of-Central-Manager","type":"heading","text":"Use of Central Manager","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"As a wrapper around ","type":"text"},{"code":"CoreBluetooth","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"‘s ","type":"text"},{"code":"CBCentralManager","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/iOS-BLE-Library\/documentation\/iOS_BLE_Library\/CentralManager","isActive":true},{"text":" cannot work unless the underlying ","type":"text"},{"code":"CBCentralManager","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is in a valid state. Mainly, it must be ","type":"text"},{"code":".poweredOn","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". If you’re familiar with BLE on Apple Platforms we’re sure you have your own strategy to account for this. You can roll your own, listening to the ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/iOS-BLE-Library\/documentation\/iOS_BLE_Library\/CentralManager\/stateChannel","isActive":true},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"PassthroughSubject","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". We offer a quick solution for ","type":"text"},{"code":"async","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" environments in the form of ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/iOS-BLE-Library\/documentation\/iOS_BLE_Library\/CentralManager\/isPoweredOn()","isActive":true},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let centralManager: CentralManager = \/\/ init CentralManager","","do {","   \/\/ Assumed async environment","   await centralManager.isPoweredOn()","","   \/\/ Bluetooth available","} catch let bleError {","   \/\/ Bluetooth unavailable","}"]},{"anchor":"Channels","type":"heading","text":"Channels","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Channels are used to pass through data from the "},{"code":"CBCentralManagerDelegate","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" methods."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"You can consider them as a reactive version of the "},{"code":"CBCentralManagerDelegate","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" methods."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In most cases, you will not need to use them directly, as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"centralManager"},{"type":"text","text":"’s methods return proper publishers. However, if you need to handle the data differently (e.g., log all the events), you can subscribe to the channels directly."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"All channels have ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Never"},{"text":" as their failure type because they never fail. Some channels, like ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CentralManager\/connectedPeripheralChannel"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CentralManager\/disconnectedPeripheralsChannel"},{"text":", send tuples with the peripheral and the error, allowing you to handle errors if needed. Despite this, the failure type remains ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Never"},{"text":", so it will not complete even if an error occurs during the connection or disconnection of the peripheral.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["centralManager.connectedPeripheralChannel","    .sink { peripheral, error in","        if let error = error {","            print(\"Error: \\(error)\")","        } else {","            print(\"New peripheral connected: \\(peripheral)\"","        }","    }","    .store(in: &cancellables)"]}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/iOS-BLE-Library\/documentation\/iOS_BLE_Library\/CentralManager"},"abstract":[{"text":"A Custom Central Manager class.","type":"text"}],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/iOS-BLE-Library\/documentation\/iOS_BLE_Library\/CentralManager\/init(centralManager:)","doc:\/\/iOS-BLE-Library\/documentation\/iOS_BLE_Library\/CentralManager\/init(centralManagerDelegate:queue:options:)"],"title":"Initializers"},{"anchor":"Instance-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/iOS-BLE-Library\/documentation\/iOS_BLE_Library\/CentralManager\/centralManager","doc:\/\/iOS-BLE-Library\/documentation\/iOS_BLE_Library\/CentralManager\/centralManagerDelegate"],"title":"Instance Properties"},{"anchor":"Scan","identifiers":["doc:\/\/iOS-BLE-Library\/documentation\/iOS_BLE_Library\/CentralManager\/stopScan()","doc:\/\/iOS-BLE-Library\/documentation\/iOS_BLE_Library\/CentralManager\/retrievePeripherals(withIdentifiers:)"],"title":"Scan"},{"anchor":"Connection","identifiers":["doc:\/\/iOS-BLE-Library\/documentation\/iOS_BLE_Library\/CentralManager\/connect(_:options:)","doc:\/\/iOS-BLE-Library\/documentation\/iOS_BLE_Library\/CentralManager\/cancelPeripheralConnection(_:)","doc:\/\/iOS-BLE-Library\/documentation\/iOS_BLE_Library\/CentralManager\/retrieveConnectedPeripherals(withServices:)"],"title":"Connection"},{"anchor":"Channels","identifiers":["do